cctext patch 0005: per-glyph font fallback.

A glyph missing from the chosen face drew as that face's .notdef box: CJK
in a Latin label, a symbol outside Noto's coverage. Faces registered with
plutovg_font_face_add_fallback (in order; at most 16; cctext-render adds
its regular faces as the manifest lists them, Noto Sans, Noto Serif, Noto
Sans Mono, then the CJK face) are tried in turn for a glyph the drawing
face lacks; the first that has it draws it, at the same em size. Kerning
applies only between glyphs of one face. Measuring goes through the same
layout, so a fallback glyph's advance is counted where it is drawn.
A face records `base` (the face whose data it shares) so one face
registered under many names is one fallback. New API:
plutovg_font_face_add_fallback, plutovg_font_face_clear_fallbacks.

Apply after 0004.

